{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q4412834","formula":"C₁₅H₂₂N₂O","hill":"C15H22N2O","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":15.0,"H":22.0,"N":2.0,"O":1.0},"names":{"en":"5-methoxy-N-methyl-N-isopropyltryptamine"},"descriptions":{"en":"5-MeO-MiPT, also known as 5-methoxy-N-methyl-N-isopropyltryptamine or by its nickname Moxy, is an atypical psychedelic drug of the tryptamine and 5-methoxytryptamine families. It has unique and unusual effects compared to other psychedelic tryptamines. At low doses, its effects include stimulation, tactile and sexual enhancement, some MDMA-like entactogenic effects, and introspective and mild perceptual changes with few or no psychedelic visuals or time dilation, whereas at higher doses, it produces 5-MeO-DMT-like classical psychedelic effects."},"fame":6,"pubchemCid":2763156,"mass":246.35,"charge":0,"smiles":"CC(C)N(C)CCC1=CNC2=C1C=C(C=C2)OC","inchikey":"HEDOODBJFVUQMS-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"N-[2-(5-methoxy-1H-indol-3-yl)ethyl]-N-methylpropan-2-amine","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"2763156","atoms":40,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":3.305,"y":-2.529,"z":0.265,"el":"O"},{"x":-3.318,"y":-0.227,"z":-0.405,"el":"N"},{"x":1.73,"y":2.716,"z":0.001,"el":"N"},{"x":-2.077,"y":0.369,"z":0.078,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.1,"y":0.674,"z":-1.073,"el":"C"},{"x":-4.229,"y":-0.492,"z":0.709,"el":"C"},{"x":0.177,"y":1.251,"z":-0.607,"el":"C"},{"x":1.349,"y":0.531,"z":-0.243,"el":"C"},{"x":2.308,"y":1.474,"z":0.134,"el":"C"},{"x":0.442,"y":2.592,"z":-0.446,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.043,"y":-1.461,"z":-1.142,"el":"C"},{"x":-5.55,"y":-1.054,"z":0.19,"el":"C"},{"x":-4.453,"y":0.793,"z":1.499,"el":"C"},{"x":1.688,"y":-0.836,"z":-0.199,"el":"C"},{"x":3.594,"y":1.116,"z":0.555,"el":"C"},{"x":2.97,"y":-1.208,"z":0.221,"el":"C"},{"x":3.907,"y":-0.246,"z":0